  "response_text": "I'm sorry to hear that you're feeling overwhelmed with your stress and the upcoming exam week. Here's a practical plan to help you manage your stress and stay focused on your studies:\n\n1. Create a realistic study schedule: Break down your study time into manageable chunks and set specific goals for each session. Make sure to include breaks and time for relaxation and rest.\n\n2. Prioritize your tasks: Identify the most important and time-sensitive tasks and focus on completing them first. This will help you stay on track and avoid feeling overwhelmed.\n\n3. Create a study environment: Find a quiet and comfortable place to study where you can focus on your work without distractions. Make sure your study space is organized and free of clutter.\n\n4. Take care of yourself: Make sure to eat well, get enough sleep, and exercise regularly. Taking care of your physical and mental health will help you stay focused and energized.\n\n5. Practice relaxation techniques: Try techniques such as deep breathing, meditation, or yoga to help reduce stress and improve your focus.\n\n6. Seek support: Talk to your teachers, classmates, or a counselor if you're feeling overwhelmed or stressed. They can provide support and guidance to help you manage your stress and stay on track.\n\n7. Stay positive: Focus on your goals and the progress you've made so far. Remember that setbacks are a normal part of the learning process, and that you can overcome them with hard work and determination.\n\nBy following this plan, you can manage your stress and stay focused on your studies during exam week. Remember to be kind to yourself and take things one step at a time.",
